From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:57:29 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 11/34] Plutonium: native fullscreen for embedded apps and
 tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts

EXO-FULLSCREEN: the browser can make a <native-window> or a tab's <embed>
its document's fullscreen element (Blink's Fullscreen API, so the app or
page is resized to the screen). Super+F toggles it for the focused embedded
window or tab; an embedded app's own xdg_toplevel.set_fullscreen and a tab
page's requestFullscreen() go the same way. The app is told it is
fullscreen while its element is. No Esc bubble for the shell's elements.

EXO-KEYS: windowBroker.setShellShortcuts() reserves key combinations the
shell handles itself; they reach the shell page while an embedded window or
tab has the keyboard.

Parked windows drop their frame and are sized directly (not fitted to the
work area); <native-window> sizes the window to its content box, ignoring
object-fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
